var ITEMS=[["What teachers do","Teachers plan lessons, deliver instruction, assess learning, and manage classrooms \u2014 shaping minds daily. It requires a bachelor's degree plus certification in most places, endless patience, and genuine love of the subje"], ["Key skills","Lesson planning with clear objectives, classroom management with consistent routines, differentiation for varied learners, formative assessment, parent communication, and reflecting on what worked. The best teachers are "], ["Tools of the trade","Whiteboard and markers, projector or smartboard, learning management system (Google Classroom, Canvas), gradebook software, quality pens, timers, and a well-organized classroom library. Digital: quiz tools, slide decks, "], ["A day in the life","Early arrival and setup, back-to-back classes with minutes between, lunch duty or meetings, afternoon planning and grading, parent emails, and professional development. The school day ends; the work often does not."], ["Getting started","Bachelor's degree, teacher preparation program, student teaching, then state certification exams. Alternative certification routes exist for career changers. Start as a substitute to test the waters."], ["Pro tips","Routines beat rules: teach procedures the first weeks. Greet students at the door. Plan more than you need. Document everything with difficult situations. Find a mentor teacher and steal their best ideas."], ["Lesson plan","Profession term \u2014 Lesson plan: The roadmap for a class period: objectives, activities, assessment."], ["Differentiation","Profession term \u2014 Differentiation: Adapting instruction for varied readiness levels."], ["Formative assessment","Profession term \u2014 Formative assessment: Checking understanding during learning."], ["Summative assessment","Profession term \u2014 Summative assessment: Evaluating learning at the end: tests, projects."], ["Rubric","Profession term \u2014 Rubric: The scoring guide for assignments."], ["IEP","Profession term \u2014 IEP: Individualized Education Program for students with disabilities."], ["504 plan","Profession term \u2014 504 plan: Accommodations for students with disabilities."], ["Bloom's taxonomy","Profession term \u2014 Bloom's taxonomy: The hierarchy from remembering to creating."], ["Scaffolding","Profession term \u2014 Scaffolding: Temporary supports removed as students master skills."], ["Classroom management","Profession term \u2014 Classroom management: The systems keeping learning orderly."], ["Bell ringer","Profession term \u2014 Bell ringer: The opening activity as class starts."], ["Exit ticket","Profession term \u2014 Exit ticket: The closing check of understanding."], ["PLC","Profession term \u2014 PLC: Professional Learning Community of collaborating teachers."], ["PD","Profession term \u2014 PD: Professional development training."], ["Tenure","Profession term \u2014 Tenure: Job protection after probationary years."], ["Substitute","Profession term \u2014 Substitute: The guest teacher covering absences."], ["Homeroom","Profession term \u2014 Homeroom: The base classroom for attendance and announcements."], ["Detention","Profession term \u2014 Detention: Supervised after-school consequence."], ["Parent-teacher conference","Profession term \u2014 Parent-teacher conference: The periodic progress meeting."]];
